      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017, Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Identification of a hiatal hernia by computed tomography (CT) scanning, and particularly with axial imaging from a coronary artery calcium score exam, is often subjective. There are several CT features that are diagnostic or at least suggestive of a hiatal hernia. As a hiatal hernia may be the etiology of a chest pain syndrome, it is important to be aware of CT findings suggestive of such."
      },
